class.description:
Movement, pathfinding, events and servers read one word per cell from the cache instead of four tile layers and a palette. The cache is compiled from a [JRPGMapData] and its tileset's baked flags ([member JRPGTilesetData.flags]):
- the passage and the sides a cell cannot be entered from or left toward come from the top-most painted tile that is neither transparent nor overhead (overhead tiles never decide). A cell where no tile decides (nothing painted, or only transparent and overhead tiles) is blocked: there is nothing to walk on;
- overhead, ladder, bush, counter and damage floor hold when any tile of the cell has them;
- the terrain tag is the top-most nonzero one; the region comes from the map.
A step toward a direction is allowed when the cell can be left on that side, the next cell can be entered from the opposite side, and the next cell is not blocked. On a looping axis the next cell wraps around; past another edge there is none.
